---------------------------------------------------------------
Apache Spark Window Functions
----------------------------------------------------------------
Window aggregate functions (aka window functions or windowed aggregates) are functions that perform a calculation over a group of records called window that are in some relation to the current record (i.e. can be in the same partition or frame as the current row).
In other words, when executed, a window function computes a value for each and every row in a window.
Spark SQL supports three kinds of window functions:
ranking functions, analytic functions and aggregate functions

Examples - 

val myRdd =
  Seq(("Lisa", "Sales", 10000, 35), ("Evan", "Sales", 32000, 38),
    ("Fred", "Engineering", 21000, 28), ("Alex", "Sales", 30000, 33),
    ("Tom", "Engineering", 23000, 33), ("Jane", "Marketing", 29000, 28),
    ("Jeff", "Marketing", 35000, 38), ("Paul", "Engineering", 29000, 23),
    ("Chloe", "Engineering", 23000, 25))
val df = myRdd.toDF("name", "dept", "salary", "age")

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Spark Window Ranking Functions
-------------------------------------------------------------------

Rank - rank() window function is used to provide a rank to the result within a window partition. This function leaves gaps in rank when there are ties.

val winSpec = Window.partitionBy("dept").orderBy("salary")
df.withColumn("rank", rank().over(winSpec)).show(false)

dense_rank- It is used to get the result with rank of rows within a window partition without any gaps. This is similar to rank() function difference being rank function leaves gaps in rank when there are ties.

df.withColumn("Dense Rank", dense_rank().over(winSpec)).show(false)

row_number - It is used to give the sequential row number starting from 1 to the result of each window partition.

df.withColumn("rowNo",row_number().over(winSpec))

ntile - It returns the relative rank of result rows within a window partition. In below example we have used 3 as an argument to ntile hence it returns ranking between 3 values (1,2 and 3)

df.withColumn("nTile", ntile(3).over(winSpec)).show()
 
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Analytics Window Functions
------------------------------------------------------------------------

cume_dist() window function is used to get the cumulative distribution of values within a window partition. This is the same as the DENSE_RANK function in SQL.
lag() window function is the same as the LAG function in SQL.
lead() window function is the same as the LEAD function in SQL.

df.withColumn("lag", lag(df.col("salary"), 1).over(winSpec))
 .withColumn("lead", lead(df.col("salary"), 1).over(winSpec))
 .withColumn("cumm_dist", cume_dist().over(winSpec)).show(false)
 
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aggregates Window Functions
------------------------------------------------------------------------

val windowDept = Window.partitionBy("dept")
val AggregateDf = df.withColumn("salaries",collect_list('salary) over windowDept)
  .withColumn("avg salary",avg('salary).over(windowDept))
  .withColumn("sum salary",sum('salary).over(windowDept))
  .withColumn("max salary",max('salary).over(windowDept))
  .withColumn("min salary",min('salary).over(windowDept))
